.TH YEET 1 "September 2026" "Bunkwerks Labs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yeet \- aggressively remove files and directories from existence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yeet
[\ \-i\ ]
[\ \-r\ ]
[\ \-f\ ]
.I FILE...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I FILE...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yeet
is a modern, high-velocity alias and wrapper for the standard 
.BR rm (1)
utility. It safely or violently ejects specified files and directories into the digital void.
.PP
When invoked, 
.B yeet
processes specified target paths with maximum prejudice. 
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Prompt before every removal. Recommended for mobile client safety.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-recursive
Recursively yeet directories and their contents into non-existence.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Ignore non-existent files and arguments, never prompt. Absolute maximum yeet.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B yeet build.log
Interactively remove a single annoying log file.
.TP
.B yeet \-rf /tmp/junk/
Recursively and forcefully vaporize an unwanted directory tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rm (1),
.BR unlink (2)
.SH AUTHOR
Kenneth Ralph Morgan
